Core Programming and Frameworks
    Python Programming: Essential for development, data processing, and integration.
    LangChain Framework: Expertise in building, orchestrating DeepAgents and subagents, prompt engineering, and multi-agent workflows.
    Large Language Models (LLMs): Understanding of how to apply and fine-tune LLMs for NLP tasks, reasoning, and decision-making within agents.

Machine Learning & Deep Learning
    Time Series Forecasting: Techniques like LSTM, GRU, Transformers for stock price prediction.
    Natural Language Processing (NLP): Sentiment analysis, text classification, entity recognition to analyze financial news and social media.
    Reinforcement Learning: Basic knowledge to implement adaptive trading strategies.
    Ensemble and Hybrid Models: Combining various prediction models for robustness.

Financial and Stock Market Knowledge
    Technical Analysis: Master technical indicators (RSI, MACD, Bollinger Bands, moving averages).
    Fundamental Analysis: Analyze financial statements, earnings, ratios, cash flows.
    Market Microstructure: Understand order book dynamics and trade execution strategies.

Data Engineering
    Real-time Data Handling: APIs for streaming stock prices, news, social media data.
    Data Preprocessing & Feature Engineering: Cleaningstock data, extracting meaningful features.
    Database Management: Storing and querying financial and market data.

Software Engineering & DevOps
    API Integration: Connecting multiple data sources and tools.
    Containerization & Cloud Deployment: Docker, AWS/GCP/Azure for scalable deployment.
    Version Control: Using Git effectively.

Visualization & Evaluation
    Data Visualization: Matplotlib, Plotly, or Dash for presenting data and model outputs.
    Model Evaluation: Metrics like RMSE, MAE for predictions, accuracy and F1 for classification.

Optional Advanced Topics
    Graph Neural Networks: For modeling relationships in market data.
    Explainable AI: Interpreting model outputs for transparency.
    Multi-Agent Systems: Designing inter-agent communication and collaboration.
    Prompt Engineering: Crafting LLM prompts specialized for stock market contexts.




THE 5‑TIMEFRAME STOCK PRICE IMPACT MODEL
(What affects prices in Minutes → Hours → Days → Weeks → Months → 1 Year)

⏱️ 1. MINUTES (Scalping & High-Frequency Trading)
Impacts price within seconds to minutes.
🔥 Focus if your goal is intraday trading.
Core Minute-Level Factors

Order Book Imbalance
Bid–Ask Spread
Market Depth
High Volume Spikes
Block Trades
Stop-Loss Hunting
Short Covering Spikes
Option Greeks (Delta/Gamma intraday hedging)
Futures Price Divergence
News Flash / Breaking Headline
Social Media Spike
Algorithmic Trading Flows
Circuit-Level Volatility

💡 This is pure microstructure behavior. Highest noise, highest risk.

🕑 2. HOURS (Intraday & Momentum Trading)
Effects last from 30 minutes to entire trading session.
🔥 Focus if you want intraday swings with slightly less noise.
Hour-Level Factors

Intraday Trend (Up/Down/Sideways)
Volume Profile (Cluster of trades)
VWAP
RSI, MACD (intraday settings)
Intraday Breakouts/Breakdowns
Big buyer/seller detection
News Reaction Continuation
Option Chain Imbalance (PCR, Max Pain intraday movement)
FII/DII intraday flow patterns
Global markets during India market hours

💡 More predictable than minutes-level; ideal for disciplined intraday traders.

📅 3. DAYS–WEEKS (Swing Trading)
These factors drive movement over 1 day → 2 weeks → 4 weeks.
🔥 Focus if you want 5–20% profits in short bursts.
Swing-Level Factors

Price Patterns (Cup-handle, W, Triangle, Flag, Channel)
Higher High / Higher Low structure
Volume Breakouts
Delivery Volume %
Short Build-up / Long Unwinding
Earnings Result Impact (short-term trend)
Macro News Reaction (rates, crude, inflation)
Sector Rotation
FII/DII Weekly Trend
Options expiry week positioning
Institutional block/bulk deals
Corporate Announcements (Buyback, Split, Bonus)

💡 Swing trading depends on momentum + patterns + institutional flows.

📆 4. MONTHS (Medium-Term Investing)
Impacts price over 3–12 months.
🔥 Focus if you want 20–60% type multi-month moves.
Medium-Term Factors

Quarterly Earnings Trend
Revenue & Profit Growth
Operating Margin Expansion
Debt Reduction
CAPEX Plans
Market Share Gains
New Product Launches
New Plants/Facilities
Management Commentary
Economic Cycle Position (expansion/recession)
Sector Growth Story
Institutional Holdings (FII/DII, Mutual Funds) trend
Corporate Governance stability
Valuation Expansion (PE re-rating)

💡 This is where real multi-bagger setups begin forming.

🗓️ 5. YEARS (Long-Term Investing)
Impacts price over 1 year – 10 years.
🔥 Focus if you want 3x–10x wealth creation.
Long-Term Factors

Consistent Revenue Growth
Strong Profit Compounding
High ROE / ROCE
Strong Free Cash Flow
Low or Reducing Debt
Competitive Moat (Tech, Brand, Patents, Cost, Scale)
Industry Tailwinds (EV, AI, Renewables, Pharma, infra)
Management Quality
Promoter Skin in the Game
Global Expansion Strategy
Strong Balance Sheet
Stable Cash Generating Business Model
Ability to survive downturns
Dominant Market Position
Governance & Transparency
Long-Term Vision & Roadmap

💡 These factors create 10–20x compounders.

🧠 THE 80/20 RULE FOR GETTING HUGE PROFITS
You don’t need all factors. You need the high-impact ones per timeframe.
For Day Trading → focus on:
✔ Order flow
✔ Intraday news
✔ Volume + Breakouts
✔ Option chain intraday flows
✔ Market sentiment
For Swing Trading → focus on:
✔ Price patterns
✔ Delivery volumes
✔ Earnings reactions
✔ Sector rotation
✔ FII/DII weekly flow
For Medium-Term (3–12 months) → focus on:
✔ Earnings + margin expansion
✔ Strong guidance
✔ Promoter/FII accumulation
✔ Industry tailwinds
For Long-Term Investing (1–5 years) → focus on:
✔ Growth + Moat
✔ Low debt
✔ FCF + ROE/ROCE
✔ Scalable business
✔ Strong management

⭐ THE MOST IMPORTANT (All Timeframes Combined)
Real-Time (Minutes–Hours):

Order-flow
Breaking news
Option hedging flows
Volume + breakouts

Short-Term (Days–Weeks):

Earnings reactions
FII/DII flows
Chart patterns + momentum

Medium-Term (Months):

Revenue & profit growth
Margin expansion
Institutional holdings growth

Long-Term (1–5 Years):

High ROE/ROCE
Moat
Visionary management
Industry tailwinds
Consistent compounding
















